        <article class="card span3 a-reg" data-card="ct-families"><header><h3>Five agreement families</h3><span class="owner a-reg">Regulator</span></header>
          <div class="body"><div class="tw"><table class="txt"><thead><tr><th>Agreement</th><th>Parties</th><th>What it secures</th><th>Key clauses</th><th>Change route</th></tr></thead><tbody>
            <tr><td>1 Charge and service rules</td><td><div class="chips"><span class="owner a-reg">Regulator</span><span class="owner a-disco">DisCo</span><span class="owner a-op">Metering Programme Operator</span></div></td><td>A lawful household metering charge and common service rules</td><td>Charge cap; replaces or reconciles the existing metering surcharge (no duplicate charging); existing entitlements credited; tiered repair limits; tightening estimated-bill caps</td><td>Regulatory decision</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2 Utility participation</td><td><div class="chips"><span class="owner a-disco">DisCo</span><span class="owner a-op">Metering Programme Operator</span></div></td><td>Common core conditions for every participating utility</td><td>Split at the token server; explicit utility contribution; feeder readiness; data sharing; ownership of meters after the term</td><td>Contract amendment or new agreement</td></tr>
            <tr><td>3 Account control and payment rules</td><td><div class="chips"><span class="owner a-gov">Government</span><span class="owner a-bank">Licensed bank</span><span class="owner a-op">Metering Programme Operator</span></div></td><td>Protected account at an existing licensed bank, executing agreed rules</td><td>Fixed payment order; daily settlement; monthly independent reconciliation; no redirection; government keeps funding authority</td><td>Operating protocol and bank mandate</td></tr>
            <tr><td>4 Regional delivery packages</td><td><div class="chips"><span class="owner a-op">Metering Programme Operator</span><span class="owner a-map">Meter providers</span><span class="owner a-supp">Suppliers</span><span class="owner a-local">Local installers</span></div></td><td>Supply, installation and maintenance in one accountable package per region</td><td>Payment on verified commissioning; repair limits; warranty and spares; import protections (below); step-in and handover</td><td>New procurement (framework)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>5 Funding</td><td><div class="chips"><span class="owner a-gov">Government</span><span class="owner a-inv">Investors &amp; DFIs</span></div></td><td>Bounded public support and, later, affordable debt</td><td>Capital grants released per batch against verified functioning meters; operating subsidy for an identified shortfall; capped expenditure; debt only where affordable cash supports it</td><td>Amendment of existing programme funding, or new agreement</td></tr>
          </tbody></table></div>
          <h4 style="margin:10px 0 4px">Alongside the five families</h4><ul class="plain"><li><b>Metering Programme Operator mandate</b> within an existing organisation: scope, delegated decisions, fee (budget plus performance part), termination rights, handover plan.</li><li><b>Customer service charter:</b> the household promise, protections and remedies.</li></ul></div></article>

        <article class="card span3 a-supp" data-card="ct-import"><header><h3>How the contracts secure imported meters</h3><span class="owner a-supp">Suppliers</span></header>
          <div class="body"><div class="tw"><table class="txt"><thead><tr><th>Risk</th><th>Clause in the delivery package</th><th>Who carries it</th></tr></thead><tbody>
            <tr><td>Currency</td><td>Price split into imported and local parts; imported part indexed to the official rate; supplier absorbs moves within ±10%, larger moves shared; price fixed per batch at call-off; forward cover for confirmed batches where affordable</td><td>Supplier first, then shared, then funding authority</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Import duty or levy</td><td>Duty status confirmed at award; change-in-law clause: a duty change after award is borne by the funding authority, not households or suppliers; meter kits assembled locally where certified</td><td>Government (it controls the duty)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Inflation</td><td>Local costs (labour, installation) indexed to CPI with a cap; annual review</td><td>Shared</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Port and delivery</td><td>Supplier delivers duty-paid to regional hubs; title and risk pass at acceptance; staged shipments; damages for late delivery</td><td>Supplier</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Quality and failure</td><td>NEMSA batch certification before payment; five-year warranty; failure-rate penalties; 2–3% spares at district hubs</td><td>Supplier</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Cash and stock</td><td>Consignment stock at hubs, paid when drawn; milestone payments (below)</td><td>Supplier holds stock; programme pays on use</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Lock-in and failure of a supplier</td><td>Open standards (STS tokens, interoperable data); portable data; dual sourcing; performance bond; step-in and handover</td><td>Supplier, with programme protection</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
          <h4 style="margin:10px 0 4px">Milestone payments</h4>
          <div class="tw"><table class="txt"><thead><tr><th>Milestone</th><th>Share of price</th><th>Trigger</th></tr></thead><tbody>
            <tr><td>Order</td><td>10–20%</td><td>Letter of credit at the licensed bank, batch confirmed</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Delivery and acceptance</td><td>40–50%</td><td>NEMSA certification and acceptance testing passed</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Verified commissioning</td><td>20–30%</td><td>Meter functioning: first token purchased, household briefed</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Retention</td><td>5–10%</td><td>Released after 12–24 months of field performance</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></article>

        <article class="card span3 a-supp" data-card="ct-factsheet"><header><h3>Fact sheet: meter supply contract</h3><span class="owner a-supp">Suppliers</span></header>
          <div class="body"><p class="lead">One-page summary of the meter supply contract inside each regional delivery package, and the clauses that protect the programme and households against change.</p>
          <div class="canvas" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(300px,1fr))">
            <div class="blk"><h3 style="color:var(--ink)">Key terms</h3>
              <div class="line"><span>Parties</span><b>Operator, supplier(s)</b></div>
              <div class="line"><span>Type</span><b>Framework, 2–3 suppliers</b></div>
              <div class="line"><span>Term</span><b>5 years + handover</b></div>
              <div class="line"><span>Orders</span><b>Quarterly call-offs</b></div>
              <div class="line"><span>Volume</span><b>Only confirmed call-offs</b></div>
              <div class="line"><span>Delivery</span><b>Duty-paid to regional hubs</b></div>
              <div class="line"><span>Standards</span><b>STS, NEMSA, open data</b></div>
              <div class="line"><span>Local share</span><b>Kit assembly target</b></div></div>
            <div class="blk"><h3 style="color:var(--ink)">Price formula</h3>
              <p class="lead" style="margin:6px 0">Batch price = local part × CPI index (capped) + imported part × FX index, fixed at call-off.</p>
              <div class="line"><span>FX move within ±10%</span><b>Supplier absorbs</b></div>
              <div class="line"><span>FX move 10–25%</span><b>Shared 50/50</b></div>
              <div class="line"><span>FX move over 25%</span><b>Review; funding authority</b></div>
              <div class="line"><span>Local costs</span><b>CPI-indexed, capped</b></div>
              <div class="line"><span>Reference rate</span><b>Official rate, call-off date</b></div></div>
            <div class="blk"><h3 style="color:var(--ink)">Protection against change</h3><ul>
              <li><b>Duty or levy change</b> after award: change-in-law clause; cost to the funding authority, not households or suppliers.</li>
              <li><b>Regulatory change</b> (standards, token rules): costed variation, agreed through the change board.</li>
              <li><b>Currency shock</b>: risk band above; forward cover for confirmed batches where affordable.</li>
              <li><b>Port or shipping delay</b>: staged shipments; delay damages; title and risk pass at acceptance.</li>
              <li><b>Supplier failure</b>: performance bond; dual sourcing; step-in and transfer to the second supplier.</li>
              <li><b>Technology change</b>: upgrade path to smart meters at agreed prices; no proprietary lock-in.</li></ul></div>
            <div class="blk"><h3 style="color:var(--ink)">Payment milestones</h3>
              <div class="line"><span>Order (letter of credit)</span><b>10–20%</b></div>
              <div class="line"><span>Delivery and NEMSA acceptance</span><b>40–50%</b></div>
              <div class="line"><span>Verified commissioning</span><b>20–30%</b></div>
              <div class="line"><span>Retention, 12–24 months</span><b>5–10%</b></div>
              <p class="lead" style="margin:6px 0 0">Consignment stock at hubs is paid only when drawn.</p></div>
            <div class="blk"><h3 style="color:var(--ink)">Quality and service</h3><ul>
              <li>Five-year warranty; replacement within the repair limits.</li>
              <li>Field failure rate above the agreed level triggers penalties or buy-back.</li>
              <li>2–3% spares held at district hubs.</li>
              <li>Batch certification by NEMSA before payment.</li></ul></div>
            <div class="blk"><h3 style="color:var(--ink)">Continuity and conduct</h3><ul>
              <li>Token keys held by the utility; software and firmware in escrow.</li>
              <li>Portable data; handover plan at exit or termination.</li>
              <li>Termination for persistent underperformance, without abandoning customers.</li>
              <li>No payments from households to supplier or installer staff.</li>
              <li>Annual price review; disputes to an independent expert, then arbitration.</li></ul></div>
          </div></div></article>

        <article class="card span3 a-bank" data-card="ct-flow"><header><h3>Payment flow</h3><span class="owner a-bank">Licensed bank</span></header>
          <div class="body">
            <div class="flowrow">
              <div class="node a-customer"><b>Household</b>Buys energy through existing channels</div><span class="arrow">→</span>
              <div class="node a-disco"><b>DisCo token server</b>Energy payment to the utility; metering charge split off</div><span class="arrow">→</span>
              <div class="node a-bank"><b>Protected account</b>Existing licensed bank, agreed rules</div><span class="arrow">→</span>
              <div class="node a-op"><b>Payment order</b>See below</div>
            </div>
            <div class="flowrow" style="margin-top:8px">
              <div class="node a-disco"><b>Utility contribution</b>Into the protected account</div>
              <div class="node a-gov"><b>Capital grants</b>Paid per verified functioning meter to delivery packages</div>
              <div class="node a-gov"><b>Operating subsidy</b>Only for an identified shortfall</div>
              <div class="node a-inv"><b>Loans (year 3+)</b>Only where affordable cash repays them</div>
            </div>
            <h4 style="margin:10px 0 4px">Payment order from the protected account</h4>
            <ol class="order"><li>Maintenance and repair obligations of the delivery packages.</li><li>Metering Programme Operator service fee: agreed budget plus a performance part (functioning service, customer outcomes, equity), reconciled with existing administration allowances.</li><li>Debt service, only once debt is introduced.</li><li>Reserve, or return to the funding authority.</li></ol>
            <p class="lead">Monthly independent reconciliation; quarterly public report. Household energy payments are utility receipts, not programme revenue.</p>
            <h4 style="margin:10px 0 4px">Cash streams</h4>
            <div class="tw"><table class="txt"><thead><tr><th>Cash stream</th><th>Purpose and treatment</th></tr></thead><tbody>
              <tr><td>Household metering charge (if lawfully approved)</td><td>Protected programme receipts; subject to affordability and duplicate-charge checks</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Explicit utility contribution</td><td>Agreed payment for the programme’s service and/or verified utility benefit</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Capital grants</td><td>Finance installation; not evidence of a self-financing business</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Operating subsidy</td><td>Funds an identified recurring service shortfall</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Operator service fee</td><td>Priced compensation for customer service, coordination, reporting and programme management</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Loan proceeds</td><td>Financing that must be repaid; not revenue</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Household energy payments</td><td>Utility receipts; not programme revenue</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
            <p class="lead" style="margin-top:6px">The operator is never paid for registrations, meter deliveries or collections alone.</p></div></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- BUSINESS MODEL -->
    <section class="view" id="v-bmc" aria-label="Business model">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.6rem;margin:0 0 2px">Business model</h2>
      <p class="lead" style="margin:0 0 12px;color:var(--muted)">The argument on one page: who the programme serves, what they receive, how it is delivered and how it is paid for. Money figures are live from the model for the selected scenario.</p>

      <article class="card a-all bm-hero"><div class="body">
        <p class="verdict" style="font-size:1.25rem;margin:0 0 6px">Functioning, maintained meters through one trusted service: no upfront payment, transparent charges, an explicit utility contribution and bounded public support.</p>
        <p class="lead" style="margin:0">Differentiation: simple access, payment transparency and maintained service, combined. The programme sells reliable metering and accountable service; it does not promise cheaper electricity.</p></div></article>

      <div class="bm-flow">
        <article class="card a-customer bm-col"><header><h3><span class="bm-n">1</span>Who we serve</h3></header><div class="body">
          <div class="bm-seg"><b>Unmetered, low-income households</b><span>Priority</span></div>
          <div class="bm-seg"><b>Other unmetered households</b><span>Priority</span></div>
          <div class="bm-seg"><b>Tenants and shared properties</b><span>Year 2</span></div>
          <div class="bm-seg"><b>Faulty or obsolete meters</b><span>Year 1</span></div>
          <div class="bm-seg"><b>Rural and hard-to-reach</b><span>Prepared from year 1</span></div>
          <div class="bm-seg muted"><b>Small businesses</b><span>Later, assessed separately</span></div></div></article>
        <div class="bm-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
        <article class="card a-op bm-col"><header><h3><span class="bm-n">2</span>What they get</h3></header><div class="body"><ul class="bm-check">
          <li>No upfront meter payment</li><li>A functioning meter, verified at commissioning</li><li>A clear explanation of what charges cover</li><li>One contact for appointments, faults and complaints</li><li>Repairs within set limits, with credits if missed</li><li>Protection against duplicate charging</li><li>No smartphone or credit score needed</li></ul></div></article>
        <div class="bm-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
        <article class="card a-agent bm-col"><header><h3><span class="bm-n">3</span>How they reach us</h3></header><div class="body">
          <div class="line"><span>Understand the offer</span><b>Community, radio, SMS</b></div>
          <div class="line"><span>Register</span><b>Agent, desk, phone, USSD</b></div>
          <div class="line"><span>Appointments</span><b>SMS or phone</b></div>
          <div class="line"><span>Buy energy</span><b>Existing vending</b></div>
          <div class="line"><span>Faults, complaints</span><b>One contact</b></div></div></article>
      </div>

      <article class="card a-op" style="margin-top:14px"><header><h3><span class="bm-n">4</span>Relationship: one owner from first contact to replacement</h3><span class="owner a-op">Meter Service Coordinator</span></header><div class="body">
        <div class="chev"><span>Understand</span><span>Register once</span><span>Assess</span><span>Appointment</span><span>Install and explain</span><span>Confirm it works</span><span>Support and repair</span></div>
        <p class="lead" style="margin:8px 0 0">Trust is measured by understanding, resolved problems and working service. Reminders support appointments and receipts; no pressure messaging or rewards for extra consumption.</p></div></article>

      <div class="bm-engine">
        <article class="card a-all"><header><h3><span class="bm-n">5</span>Partners</h3></header><div class="body"><div class="chips">
          <span class="owner a-disco">Utilities (common conditions)</span><span class="owner a-map">Regional delivery packages</span><span class="owner a-bank">Licensed bank</span><span class="owner a-gov">Government funding</span><span class="owner a-reg">Regulator, NEMSA</span><span class="owner a-agent">Vending channels, telcos</span><span class="owner a-customer">Community organisations</span></div></div></article>
        <article class="card a-all"><header><h3><span class="bm-n">6</span>Activities</h3></header><div class="body"><ul class="plain"><li>Onboarding and readiness</li><li>Procurement and installation</li><li>Payment reconciliation</li><li>Maintenance and complaints</li></ul></div></article>
        <article class="card a-all"><header><h3><span class="bm-n">7</span>Resources</h3></header><div class="body"><ul class="plain"><li>Trained staff and installers</li><li>Customer and asset register</li><li>Spares and regional service</li><li>Protected accounts, working capital</li></ul></div></article>
      </div>

      <article class="card a-inv" style="margin-top:14px"><header><h3><span class="bm-n">8</span>Money: what it costs and who pays (15 years, today’s prices)</h3><span class="owner a-inv">Investors &amp; DFIs</span></header><div class="body">
        <svg class="chart" id="ch-bmmoney" viewBox="0 0 600 150" role="img" aria-label="Lifetime cost and who pays"></svg>
        <div class="two" style="margin-top:6px"><div id="bmCostLeg"></div><div id="bmPayLeg"></div></div>
